  displayTitle: Convention Center
  location: In front of reception
  transformations: 0000000004000000
  description: "The Kigali Convention Centre opened in July 2016 and quickly became a landmark of the city. German architect Roland Dieterle designed it so that Kigali would have a building people recognise at a glance.

Its dome was inspired by the round houses of Rwandan tradition, such as the dome-shaped King's Palace.

The dome is a steel frame covered in a see-through skin and stands close to 40 metres high. The main hall underneath can hold up to 2,600 people.

At night, lights turn the dome blue, yellow and green, the colours of the Rwandan flag. Since 2024 it has also appeared on the 5,000 franc banknote.

AR experience by Brian. For the story behind the mural itself, ask ALU guest relations."
  captions:
  - Watch the dome rise out of the wall.
  - Tap the dome to change the lights, the tower cups for day or night, and the plant
    to make it bloom.
  scanHint: Stand about 3 m in front of the mural so the dome and tower fit on the
    screen.
